<title>USA: MidAmerican Energy chairman retires.</title>
<headline>MidAmerican Energy chairman retires.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>MidAmerican Energy Holdings Co said Russell Christiansen will retire as chairman effective May 31.</p>
<p>Stanley Bright, president and chief executive officer, will assume the additional duties of chairman, the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p>These management changes were outlined in a succession plan announced about three years ago when the merger which formed MidAmerican was announced. Midwest Resources Inc and Iowa-Illinois Gas and Electric Co merged July 1, 1995 to form MidAmerican Energy.</p>
<p>MidAmerican Energy, Iowa's largest utility, provides electric service to 642,000 customers and natural gas service to 610,000 customers in Iowa, Illinois, Nebraska and South Dakota.</p>
<p>--((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
